{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeSqueeze","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeSqueeze","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeSaddle"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_log_kashaev_vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_log_kashaev_vol","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSqueeze.lean#L270-L282","doc":"**The figure-eight volume-conjecture limit, machine-proved (E5d).**\n`(2π/N)·log ⟨4₁⟩_N → VOL_4_1 = 2·Cl₂(π/3)` — the Kashaev–Murakami–\nMurakami statement for `4₁`, proved in the literature by Andersen–Hansen /\nOhtsuki and here by the elementary Riemann-sum squeeze of the saddle\nprogram (E1 + E5a + E5c + E2/E3), with the exact transcendental target\nafter the qou-yf47 statement repair. Discharges the\n`VolumeConjecture41` sorry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_two_pi_log_kashaev","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_two_pi_log_kashaev","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSqueeze.lean#L118-L268","doc":"**E5d — the squeeze (sorry-free).** The scaled Kashaev log,\n`(2π/N)·log ⟨4₁⟩_N`, tends to `2·Cl₂(π/3) = Vol(4₁)`. (bean qou-f248) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.F_le_half_vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.F_le_half_vol","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSqueeze.lean#L92-L116","doc":"**The grid Clausen primitive never exceeds half the volume.** For any\ninterior grid point `1 ≤ k ≤ N − 1`,\n`F(kπ/N) = −clausen(2kπ/N)/2 ≤ Cl₂(π/3)/2` — the E3 global-minimum bound\ntransported through the series↔integral bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevProd_pos","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSqueeze.lean#L70-L90","doc":"The Kashaev product is strictly positive for `k < N` (each `4 sin²` factor\nis positive on the interior grid). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_deviation_le_masterErr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_deviation_le_masterErr","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSqueeze.lean#L61-L68","doc":"E5c-4 in `masterErr` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_masterErr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_masterErr","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSqueeze.lean#L56-L59","doc":"E5c-5 in `masterErr` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.masterErr_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.masterErr_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSqueeze.lean#L48-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.masterErr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.masterErr","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeSqueeze.lean#L39-L46","doc":"The E5c-4 master deviation error\n`E(N) = |F(π/N)| + (π/N)|f(π/N)| + 7·(π/N)(|f(π/N)| + log 2)` — the\nk-independent bound of `abs_deviation_le`, packaged as a named function\nfor the squeeze. ","signatureChunk":0}]}